. He created half of his pantheon with his lust, and numerous other central figures to his mythology. Also I think the more vital aspect of those stories wasn't the relationship between Zeus and his wife or lover or victim, but rather as a fertility figure spreading his seed everywhere it could be spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:19:30-07:00","id":908838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908835#post908835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that rape is in any way important to his myth though, we look at Zeus today and say &quot;wow he sure liked to turn in to golden showers or swans and go rape strangers&quot; because that is we see the ancient world through our more modern and developed morals, morals they did not share. But thousands of years ago when these myths were being formed the greater intent was probably to tell stories of Zeus' great passions and how they get him and those around him in trouble.<br /> <br /> People weren't supposed to look at his acts and say &quot;wow don't be a rapist&quot; because they didn't care about that, they were supposed to look at him and say &quot;wow better show some self control&quot;. I doubt Zeus is still going around raping people in the modern setting of Scion's World because that's not the core of his myth, but is he still a reckless philanderer like he was thousands of years ago? probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never looked at it that away;I think you're right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T20:59:26-07:00","id":908864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908837#post908837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Creator then, rather than Lover. He created half of his pantheon with his lust, and numerous other central figures to his mythology. Also I think the more vital aspect of those stories wasn't the relationship between Zeus and his wife or lover or victim, but rather as a fertility figure spreading his seed everywhere it could be spread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah you are probably right, creator is a better fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T21:05:19-07:00","id":908868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908835#post908835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that rape is in any way important to his myth though, we look at Zeus today and say &quot;wow he sure liked to turn in to golden showers or swans and go rape strangers&quot; because that is we see the ancient world through our more modern and developed morals, morals they did not share. But thousands of years ago when these myths were being formed the greater intent was probably to tell stories of Zeus' great passions and how they get him and those around him in trouble.<br /> <br /> People weren't supposed to look at his acts and say &quot;wow don't be a rapist&quot; because they didn't care about that, they were supposed to look at him and say &quot;wow better show some self control&quot;. I doubt Zeus is still going around raping people in the modern setting of Scion's World because that's not the core of his myth, but is he still a reckless philanderer like he was thousands of years ago? probably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Zeus raping people may not have been the core of his myth, but it was heavily structured around it. Most of the time, Zeus didn't even try taking responsibility for his actions or bother to apologize for them later. Acting as more of a &quot;Do as I say, not as I do&quot; kind of Leader. If this were Game of Thrones, Zeus would be King Geoffrey, a petulant child who had been granted way too much power. Hell, he even betrayed the allies who helped him out during the first Titan War!<br /> <br /> <br /> So with that in mind, I would say maybe swap out Lover for Trickster?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T22:47:00-07:00","id":908904,"title":"","content":"First there is no such thing as a standard set of Greek Myths, as practically every town and region could have their own myths of the Gods. The Athenian tended to be the most common myths. But there were plenty others from Argos, to Sparta, to Thebes, to the later Hellenistic Kingdoms who all tended to have their own distinct view of the gods and goddesses. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, from what I have read by others there wasn't really a word for rape, the concept existed though but there was no word for it. We do know rape was punished because the athenian lawgiver Solon had rape punishable at a 100 drachmas, unless he was seduced then it was 20 drachmas. A chicken or a bushel of wheat btw was only a drachma, so if you raped someone after being seduced you could pay the price of 20 chickens. The ancient greeks were misogynistic, especially the athenians. <br /> <br /> More related to scion, there is a myth in greek mythology that does directly deal with Rape and its Conquesnces: the Judgement of Areas. Where Halirrhothios, one of the sons of Poseidon tried to or did rape Ares's daughter, Alkippe. Ares in return slew Halirrhothios for his action. Where upon he was tried by the gods and acquitted of his crime. <br /> <br /> As for my own views of the myths, I do not regard Zeus raping those he sleeps with. He seduces and has plenty of affairs with people, but it is consensual. More over a lot of the stories are to explain why things exist. That is what it seems the various lovers of Zeus were. Kings would trace their lineage back to Zeus as a way to back up their legitimacy. It was also used to explain how other gods, monsters, creatures and heroes came to be. <br /> <br /> There is after all the festival of the theogamia which celebrates the marriage and love between Zeus and Hera. For all his sleeping around, Hera seems to be is main love; doesn't mean that she likes him sleeping around though. Of course my view is different being that I actually worship the Theoi. But as mentioned there is no such thing as a standard greek myth. For example, in one myth Hera is outraged at Athena's birth, another she is rejoicing over it. <br /> <br /> As for callings I would give him the following: Lover, Leader, and Warrior. Love is the most obvious one. Leader, not only as the king of the gods, but the god who handles the duties of a leader, a king. Warrior due to his his war with the titans and Typhon. Not to mention there are several titles that explicit list war or warlike activities for Zeus; which ties back in kingly duties, a king must know war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T22:59:12-07:00","id":908911,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to see how keeping the amount of Callings to exactly 3 per god might lead to some shoehorning. There are four or five that definitely apply to Zeus, six for Odin, and I can think of several major gods that really don't fit more than two.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also misread, thanks for the clarification Danelsan that there is a MAXIMUM of 3 per god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":1093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","user":"Arlecchino","date":". 06-07-2016, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:30:32-07:00","id":908927,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't exactly say Zeus' lovers were consensual. All they did was <i>touch him</i> while he appeared in the form of a swan, pile of gold, est. Upon making physical contact, they were pregnant with his children.<br /> <br /> <br /> Come to think of it, what does the Liminal calling mean? I tried to look up the definition and found this<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>1</b>.<br /> of or relating to a transitional or initial stage of a process.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>2</b>.<br /> occupying a position at, or on both sides of, a boundary or threshold.</span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:49:53-07:00","id":908936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callings open dev post</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You start with a dot in a Calling and a Calling Path. Heroes <b>can </b>maintain one Calling; Demigods, two; and Gods, three. They\u2019re added to by Transfigurations, or undergoing a Crisis of Calling that allows you to double down or shy away from tying yourself to an archetype</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that is not how it was meant to be read, but unless Transfigurations (and/or somehow Crisis of Calling) are mandatory, this bit reads to me as upper limits. If neither is <i>sure </i>to happen, a God could have a single Calling by never going trough the processes that allows more to be added.<br /> <br /> As for many gods needing more than 3...I don't know, we might be applying the Callings too &quot;generously&quot;. We don't know exactly what paths each confers and all the associated Purviews and so on. Odin is a warrior among other things, but not all warriors are necessarily Warriors as far as Callings go, for instance.<br /> <br /> And while I'm already speculating: seems unlikely, but perhaps it is possible for a character to follow different Callings while in different Mantles (if those are still a thing)?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(also, what is up with this forum's software that accepts transfiguration and purview as words, but not their plurals XD )</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:55:41-07:00","id":908942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908927#post908927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, what does the Liminal calling mean? I tried to look up the definition and found this<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>1</b>.<br /> of or relating to a transitional or initial stage of a process.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>2</b>.<br /> occupying a position at, or on both sides of, a boundary or threshold.</span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>From the Ask Neall thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908454#post908454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Neall, the blog post looks brilliant. I was hesitant about archtype-esque ideas, but this looks to qualm my worries about them. What instantly stood out to me (asides from the funny Lugh blurb) was the mention of &quot;Liminal&quot; as one of the Paths. Instantaneously you had my attention with this, totally unexpected, and yet from the name I can see that it is something absolutely core to myth that was unfortunately left out of Scion 1E.<br /> <br /> Could you let us know more about the &quot;Liminal&quot; Path and some Gods or Goddesses who embody it? My immediate thought was Loki, Tezcat, Ishtar, and Radegast as the outside-insiders, but I wouldn't want to assume anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=908672#post908672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've decided to put outsider-insider status more on tricksters, but a large part of &quot;divided deities&quot; or ones who are clearly of two worlds are Liminal. Ishtar, but also Hermes or Janus.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the comments on the Callings open dev post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does Liminal encompass?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Neall Price</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messengers, heralds, gods of boundaries and psychopomps.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T23:57:03-07:00","id":908943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908936#post908936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe that is not how it was meant to be read, but unless Transfigurations (and/or somehow Crisis of Calling) are mandatory, this bit reads to me as upper limits. If neither is <i>sure </i>to happen, a God could have a single Calling by never going trough the processes that allows more to be added.<br /> <br /> As for many gods needing more than 3...I don't know, we might be applying the Callings too &quot;generously&quot;. We don't know exactly what paths each confers and all the associated Purviews and so on. Odin is a warrior among other things, but not all warriors are necessarily Warriors as far as Callings go, for instance.<br /> <br /> And while I'm already speculating: seems unlikely, but perhaps it is possible for a character to follow different Callings while in different Mantles (if those are still a thing)?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(also, what is up with this forum's software that accepts transfiguration and purview as words, but not their plurals XD )</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just read the front page explanation and apparently your Calling is supposed to be what type of God your character is becoming, not what their history involves. So you may be right in applying Callings too generously. We need to think less about what they did in mythology, and more about how they were depicted by their followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:11:31-07:00","id":909027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings#post908618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we know that (in Hero, at least) there will be ten Pantheons who each have between seven and twelve deities, and that each of those deities has three of the eleven Callings, one of which is passed on to their Scions. I figured it might be fun to try and puzzle out likely Callings for some major gods, but didn't want to fill up the Ask Neall thread with it. To recap:<br /> <br /> Pantheons: Norse, Hindu, Japanese, Algonquian, Egyptian, Yoruban, Chinese, Aztec, Greco-Roman, and Irish.<br /> Callings: Creator, Guardian, Healer, Hunter, Judge, Leader, Liminal, Lover, Sage, Trickster, and Warrior.<br /> <br /> My knowledge is mostly of the Egyptian gods, so I'll start with them. Azar/Osiris is obvious both a Leader and a Liminal god, existing as king of the underworld, but the third is a little tougher to pin down; I think that he and his wife, Aset/Isis, likely share being Lovers. Aset's a goddess of magic and names, so Sage is likely, and her ability to revive her dead and dismembered husband marks her as a Healer. <br /> <br /> Ra and Heru/Horus overlap significantly, but are certainly both Leaders and Warriors; Heru is also a god of the hunt, while Ra is sometimes the creator god. Sutek/Set is a Trickster in that he lies outside the order of the traditional Egyptian structure, and is probably both a Guardian (in his role as protector of the solar barge) and a Warrior. Anpu/Anubis is the easiest to classify, as a Liminal/Guardian/Judge. Djehuty/Thoth is a blatant Sage, as the inventor of writing and patron of sciences, but he's also a Judge and arbitrator between the gods and a Guardian of the solar barge. <br /> <br /> That takes us up to six or seven gods already, and I'd be surprised if they get too many more than the minimum. Bast and/or Sekhmet (will the writing team combine them, I wonder?) have to make it in, and I think Ptah and Hathor are probably as well. I'm afraid Sobek is a little too niche, which bums me out, but you never know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sobek created all of the world's rivers,correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:16:32-07:00","id":909030,"title":"","content":"It was also the god of the Nile, 