Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Zeus:</b> Leader, Warrior, LOVER<br /> <br /> I chose Warrior for Zeus, because of how he defeated Typhon in single combat. A monster who, as far as I can tell, was the size of a planet. <i>His head reached the stars and his arms spanned the horizon.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Amaterasu:</b> Leader, Sage, Guardian</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd give Zeus Judge before Warrior. He is the God of Law and Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:57:41-07:00","id":909704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908927#post908927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't exactly say Zeus' lovers were consensual. All they did was <i>touch him</i> while he appeared in the form of a swan, pile of gold, est. Upon making physical contact, they were pregnant with his children.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're definitely going to need to site a source for me on that one. Because nothing I've read has ever cast Leta having just touched the swan, or Hera as having just touched the Cuckoo...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:06:19-07:00","id":909710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908904#post908904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for my own views of the myths, I do not regard Zeus raping those he sleeps with. He seduces and has plenty of affairs with people, but it is consensual. More over a lot of the stories are to explain why things exist. That is what it seems the various lovers of Zeus were. Kings would trace their lineage back to Zeus as a way to back up their legitimacy. It was also used to explain how other gods, monsters, creatures and heroes came to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed the reason for the myths - but there are quite a few explicit unambiguous rapes. The ancient Greeks might not have thrown the world around for Zeus, but that's because as horrible misogynists, their conception of rape of a woman was about violating the rights of another man (a woman's husband, or an unmarried woman's father or oldest brother, etc)*. Since Zeus's rights superseded those of any mortal, he was by definition incapable of violating someone else's property.<br /> <br /> *This is fairly normal in the Ancient Mediterranean. Tanakh (the so called &quot;Old Testament&quot; for Christians) says the rapist of an unmarried woman should pay her father the bride's price and marry her to make restitution. Even up into modern times, rape of a woman was so strongly conceived as the violation of a man's property rights rather than of a woman's own body that the law in the western world didn't start recognizing a man forcing himself on his wife against her will as being rape until the late 20th Century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:37:24-07:00","id":909743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909704#post909704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're definitely going to need to site a source for me on that one. Because nothing I've read has ever cast Leta having just touched the swan, or Hera as having just touched the Cuckoo...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's the stories as I read them back around middle school / early high school years. I read them from a book, not a site, because internet wasn't as big a thing as it is now. Zeus poured himself through a key hole in the shape of gold coins and upon scooping a handful of said coins, the girl was pregnant.<br /> <br /> And during the swan story, the girl is described as having reached out to pet Zeus and was impregnated that way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-07-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:43:08-07:00","id":909751,"title":"","content":"Your version was a bit Baulderized I believe. In the original sources it wasn't just a touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:52:51-07:00","id":909761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909751#post909751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your version was a bit Baulderized I believe. In the original sources it wasn't just a touch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well as we've discussed previously, there's no unified version of the myths. So I suppose it's possible to get the story mixed up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909710#post909710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That is indeed the reason for the myths - but there are quite a few explicit unambiguous rapes. The ancient Greeks might not have thrown the world around for Zeus, but that's because as horrible misogynists, their conception of rape of a woman was about violating the rights of another man (a woman's husband, or an unmarried woman's father or oldest brother, etc)*. Since Zeus's rights superseded those of any mortal, he was by definition incapable of violating someone else's property.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*This is fairly normal in the Ancient Mediterranean. Tanakh (the so called &quot;Old Testament&quot; for Christians) says the rapist of an unmarried woman should pay her father the bride's price and marry her to make restitution. Even up into modern times, rape of a woman was so strongly conceived as the violation of a man's property rights rather than of a woman's own body that the law in the western world didn't start recognizing a man forcing himself on his wife against her will as being rape until the late 20th Century.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">True. Remember that the world was a very different place thousands of years ago. What might be considered abhorrent today was seen as perfectly acceptable back then. Like, for example, slavery. That shit was all over the world back then, and still is in less modernized countries.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyways, a culture who didn't consider lesbian relationships to be real sex probably isn't the best source to rely on when it comes to rape stories.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-07-2016, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:16:53-07:00","id":909814,"title":"","content":"Back to the topic at hand, I don't know how easy it is to switch callings, but I can see Zeus replacing Warrior with Judge after the fall of the (1st) Titanomachy. I still say Creator and Leader as his other two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:28:01-07:00","id":909817,"title":"","content":"My thinking on the Theoi:<br /> <br /> Zeus: Leader, Creator, Judge<br /> Hera: Lover, Judge?<br /> Ares: Warrior<br /> Hephaestus: Creator <br /> Hermes: Liminal, Trickster (maybe switched around)<br /> Dionysus: Liminal, Lover<br /> Artemis: Hunter <br /> Apollo: Sage, Healer<br /> Athena: Sage, Judge, Warrior<br /> Persephone: Liminal <br /> Aphrodite: Lover<br /> Demeter: Creator <br /> Hades: Judge<br /> <br /> I'll probably change when I have time to really peruse the descriptions, but these are my initial thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:35:04-07:00","id":909856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909817#post909817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thinking on the Theoi:<br /> <br /> Zeus: Leader, Creator, Judge<br /> Hera: Lover, Judge?<br /> Ares: Warrior<br /> Hephaestus: Creator <br /> Hermes: Liminal, Trickster (maybe switched around)<br /> Dionysus: Liminal, Lover<br /> Artemis: Hunter <br /> Apollo: Sage, Healer<br /> Athena: Sage, Judge, Warrior<br /> Persephone: Liminal <br /> Aphrodite: Lover<br /> Demeter: Creator <br /> Hades: Judge<br /> <br /> I'll probably change when I have time to really peruse the descriptions, but these are my initial thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also remember that the Theoi are the Roman pantheon in addition to being the Greek, and I think it's been said that an Etruscan deity or two might sneak in. While Ares is certainly a Warrior, Mars may well dabble in Creator or Leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:50:43-07:00","id":909864,"title":"","content":"Can't think of Zeus doing a lot of creation (except people via sex) in the myths. So &quot;Creator&quot; seems an odd call on him to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T22:52:19-07:00","id":909866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909817#post909817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thinking on the Theoi:<br /> <br /> Zeus: Leader, Creator, Judge<br /> Hera: Lover, Judge?<br /> Ares: Warrior<br /> Hephaestus: Creator<br /> Hermes: Liminal, Trickster (maybe switched around)<br /> Dionysus: Liminal, Lover<br /> Artemis: Hunter<br /> Apollo: Sage, Healer<br /> Athena: Sage, Judge, Warrior<br /> Persephone: Liminal<br /> Aphrodite: Lover<br /> Demeter: Creator<br /> Hades: Judge<br /> <br /> I'll probably change when I have time to really peruse the descriptions, but these are my initial thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since Liminals are all about psychopomps/travel/borders/etc, it's actually much stronger for Hermes than Dionysus. In fact with the &quot;outsider&quot; and &quot;chaos&quot; association for Trickster, that'd actually be stronger for Dionysus than Hermes, even though Hermes is nominally the biggest deceiver/thief/prankster among the Olympians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T00:26:10-07:00","id":909896,"title":"","content":"I'm basing my definition of &quot;Trickster&quot; on Lewis Hyde's fantastic book &quot;Trickster Makes This World&quot; (can't recommend enough), and I'm not seeing Dionysus fitting any definition of the archetype, aside from lust. And since he's usually depicted as having that lust satiated fairly quickly, he never goes through the whole clever Trickster process. Hermes, however, is every definition of a Trickster at least somewhere in the myths that center around him.<br /> <br /> (Admittedly, I haven't read or watched Euripides' The Bacchae in many years, and I vaguely remember Dionysus being Tricksterish in that)<br /> <br /> And I'm sticking to my guns with Zeus as Creator. Maybe even as his second archetype. If he does one thing, it's spread his seed and sow generations of gods and heroes. Some gods create with their gardens, or their hammers and anvils. Zeus creates with his ****. (And thigh, and forehead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T00:34:00-07:00","id":909897,"title":"","content":"I very much doubt fathering Scions is what the Creator archetype is talking about.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that Dionysus isn't a clever deceiver like Hermes, but he does have the &quot;outsider figure who introduces new ways of thinking&quot; from said book aspect down pat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T00:42:23-07:00","id":909905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909897#post909897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I very much doubt fathering Scions is what the Creator archetype is talking about.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that Dionysus isn't a clever deceiver like Hermes, but he does have the &quot;outsider figure who introduces new ways of thinking&quot; from said book aspect down pat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just throwing this out there, but Dionysus was originally a hermaphrodite, if I'm not mistaken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, he's the god of wine, orgies and festivities. I'm pretty sure he's at the very least a competent prankster, if not an outright trickster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T00:56:18-07:00","id":909909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909897#post909897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you that Dionysus isn't a clever deceiver like Hermes, but he does have the &amp;quot;outsider figure who introduces new ways of thinking&amp;quot; from said book aspect down pat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I suppose you could argue that the deceptive effects of wine are his doing. As are the masks of theatre.<br /> <br /> Anyway, not to belabor a point, but I'm curious what the creator archetype DOES encompass. World creation? Agriculture and fertility? Industry and production? The arts? Childbirth? All of the above?<br /> <br /> I also notice I didn't give any if them the &quot;Guardian&quot; calling. Athena already has 3, and the others seem a stretch. What do y'all think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T01:31:30-07:00","id":909916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909905#post909905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just throwing this out there, but Dionysus was originally a hermaphrodite, if I'm not mistaken. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, he's the god of wine, orgies and festivities. I'm pretty sure he's at the very least a competent prankster, if not an outright trickster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gender-bending definitely, and it falls under his purview. I'm not aware of any surviving source that refers to him having anything other than male-labeled anatomy - but he has lived as a girl/woman as well as a man, and acts as patron God of those who transgress assigned gender barriers.<br /> <br /> Sexuality speaking that gender-transgression theme plays out in him being the only Olympian God who bottoms - as the position a man takes in gay sex is entirely based on social rank in the Ancient Greek perspective, and someone as high ranked as a god being penetrated was an unthinkable transgression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-08-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T05:40:39-07:00","id":909997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=909909#post909909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I also notice I didn't give any if them the &quot;Guardian&quot; calling. Athena already has 3, and the others seem a stretch. What do y'all think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, Athena is a goddess of strategy and tactics, rather than the act of fighting like Ares is. So I would say drop Warrior and use Guardian, instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:43:40-07:00","id":910293,"title":"","content":"A guessing game! Neat!<br /> Norse:<br /> Loki: Trickster, Liminal, Creator (due to inventiveness, the many objects the gods possess because of him, and the fishing net story. First two callings are self-explanatory.)<br /> Odin: Leader, Liminal, Warrior (god of the warrior elite, but also a transgressor, shapechanger and wanderer.)<br /> Thor: Guardian, Warrior, Liminal (Defends the boundaries of civilization, \u2018nuff said.)<br /> Freyr: Lover, Healer, Hunter (Honestly, for a fertility god he can be fierce, plus the association with the wild boar)<br /> Freya: Warrior, Liminal, Lover (Okay, she needs Sage too, as the resident Seidr-woman, but there is not enough room.)<br /> Frigg: Sage, Guardian, Judge (Mystery, protection, truth)<br /> Heimdall: Guardian, Warrior, Liminal (So very straightforward. Guards one of the most important borders, fights, wanders)<br /> Tyr: Warrior, Judge, (Either liminal because of Fenris, or guardian)<br /> Bragi: Creator, Sage, Judge(because poetry is associated with truth?)<br /> Idunn: Creator, Healer, Guardian (Well, the Thiazzi incident shows she needs others to look out for her, but she was able to protect the apples)<br /> Baldr: Healer, Guardian, Liminal (third calling because he is a death-and-rebirth figure, but a case for Judge can be made, due to Forseti)<br /> Skadi: Hunter, Judge, Warrior (Don\u2019t mess with her. Just don\u2019t.)<br /> <br /> Hindu:<br /> Brahma: Creator, Judge, Sage (Is there such a thing as \u201ctoo obvious\u201d?)<br /> Vishnu: Guardian, Healer/Warrior, Trickster (Can we just say the second Calling changes depending on what is necessary right now?)<br /> Shiva: Judge, Liminal , Hunter (He represents an unreachable truth/standard holy men aspire to, transcends every boundary, and is the Lord of the Wild to boot.)<br /> Uma: Judge, Guardian, Healer/Warrior (How about *you* try waking up Kali)<br /> Lakshmi: Creator, Healer, Lover (Successful, lucky, kind and devoted)<br /> Saraswati: Sage, Creator, Judge (Lady of knowledge, truth and inspiration)<br /> Indra: Warrior, Guardian, Leader (A mighty bull among gods)<br /> Agni: Liminal, Judge, Sage (Everybody\u2019s guest, all-knower, seven-tongued, poet)<br /> Ganesha: Sage, Guardian, Judge (Is giving Judge to gods associated with the discerning of truth even justified? I think it is!)<br /> Varuna: Judge, Liminal, Guardian (all about Rta. In terrible mood because of Mitra\u2019s absence.)<br /> Yama: Judge, Liminal, Sage (The Nachiketa story shows he is associated with knowledge and wisdom)<br /> Ganga: Healer, Lover, Guardian (Pure, protective, irresistible)<br /> <br /> Japanese:<br /> Amaterasu: Leader, Judge, Guardian (This sun goddess has no time for bullshit)<br /> Susanoo: Warrior, Liminal, Guardian (Fights, doesn\u2019t play by the rules, protects the land from Yamato no Orochi)<br /> Tsukiyomi: Liminal, Sage, Judge (Moon god. Very particular about formalities. And food, apparently.)<br /> Izanagi: Creator, Guardian, Healer (Creation, purification, protection - kinda straightforward?)<br /> Izanami: Liminal, Creator, Judge (for vindictiveness)<br /> Hachiman: Warrior, Guardian, Leader(must have for military commanders)<br /> Fujin/Raijin: Warrior, Liminal, Guardian (or does Trickster fit better?)<br /> Inari: Liminal, Creator, Healer (Gender boundaries? Never heard of those)<br /> Okuninushi: Guardian, Leader, Liminal (Relinquished control of the land, but not the responsibility)<br /> Kannon: Healer, Guardian, Creator (Overworked, but can\u2019t stop)<br /> Ame no Uzume: Liminal, Trickster, Creator (Stirring up trouble and can\u2019t stop)<br /> Ryujin: Liminal, Guardian, Sage (Mysterious dragon beneath the waves. Hard to pin down.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 06-17-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:23:59-07:00","id":911143,"title":"","content":"The Tuatha are difficult to guess, as their only extant stories are from well after they were actually worshipped, written down by Christian priests who wrote about them as descendants of Noah. We don't know what archetypes they were worshipped as.<br /> <br /> You just have to assume Callings based on how you want to interpret their actions in those stories, (Nuada as Leader and Dian Cecht as Healer are fairly easy, Bres and Midir not so much).<br /> <br /> NOTE: I'm not saying Neall et. al. won't make awesome, playable, interesting interpretations of the Tuatha's Callings, just that it's not super easy to predict which creative direction they'll take, compared to better documented Pantheons like the Theoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":1093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","user":"Arlecchino","date":". 06-10-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:45:16-07:00","id":911858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=911143#post911143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tuatha are difficult to guess, as their only extant stories are from well after they were actually worshipped, written down by Christian priests who wrote about them as descendants of Noah. We don't know what archetypes they were worshipped as.<br /> <br /> You just have to assume Callings based on how you want to interpret their actions in those stories, (Nuada as Leader and Dian Cecht as Healer are fairly easy, Bres and Midir not so much).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true, but we must make do with the sources we do have.<br /> Say, let us talk about Midir. Love troubles seem to be an important part of his legend. As well as the fact that he is a great ruler in the Otherworld - does this mean Liminal, Leader or both? How about the tricks he is so fond of? Using brains before brawn might mean he is a Trickster, too. Which would be very interesting, because that's an unexpected archetype for such a dignified and lofty figure.<br /> Incidentally...<br /> <br /> <br /> Irish:<br /> The Dagda: Leader, Warrior, Liminal<br /> The Morrigan: Warrior, Liminal, Sage<br /> Dian Cecht: Healer, Judge, Sage<br /> Nuada Airgetlam: Leader, Guardian, Warrior<br /> Lugh Lamhfhada: Leader, Warrior, Creator<br /> Brighid: Creator, Healer, Guardian<br /> Goibniu: Creator, Healer, ? Boann: Sage, Liminal, Creator<br /> Oghma: Sage, Judge, Warrior<br /> Aengus: Lover, Creator, ?<br /> Manannan Mac Lir: Liminal, Judge, Sage<br /> Midir: Liminal, Lover, Trickster?<br /> <br /> <br /> Aztec:<br /> Huitzilopochtli: Warrior, Leader, Guardian<br /> Tezcatlipoca: Liminal, Warrior, Trickster (Yes, Sage is also necessary, but... Only three slots. Actually, is there a calling that wouldn't fit Tezcatlipoca? Healer, I guess...)<br /> Quetzalcoatl: Sage, Creator, Leader (as shown in the fall of Tollan story)<br /> Xipe-Totec: Creator, Healer, Liminal<br /> Tlaloc: Creator, Liminal, Guardian (Is the third one a stretch?) Chalchiuhtlicue: Creator, Healer, Judge<br /> Tlazolteotl: Judge, Liminal, Lover (Interesting combo)<br /> Huehueteotl: Creator, Guardian, Liminal<br /> Xochiquetzal: Lover, Healer, Liminal (Passions, blooming life, transitions)<br /> Xochipilli: Lover, Liminal, Trickster<br /> Mictlantecuhtli: Liminal, Judge, Guardian<br /> Mixcoatl: Hunter, Warrior, Liminal<br /> <br /> Greco-Roman:<br /> Zeus: Leader, Judge, Guardian<br /> Hera: Judge, Guardian, Leader<br /> Poseidon: Liminal, Creator, Leader<br /> Athene: Guardian, Creator, Warrior<br /> Apollo: Creator, Sage, Healer<br /> Hermes: Liminal, Trickster, Sage (hey there, Trismegistos)<br /> Artemis: Hunter, Guardian, Liminal<br /> Hephaistos: Creator, Liminal, Judge?<br /> Dionysos: Liminal, Creator, Hunter<br /> Aphrodite: Lover, Creator, Trickster<br /> Ares: Warrior, Guardian, Leader<br /> Demeter: Creator, Guardian, Judge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","user":"Xanthias","date":". 06-10-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:17:27-07:00","id":915837,"title":"","content":"I think it's a case where if you have Liminal and Trickster at the same time you can probably settle for one or the other. Instead of having Liminal Trickster Sage Odin we can maybe just go Liminal Judge Leader (or Warrior? I don't recall off the top of my head).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:45:38-07:00","id":916319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=915837#post915837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a case where if you have Liminal and Trickster at the same time you can probably settle for one or the other. Instead of having Liminal Trickster Sage Odin we can maybe just go Liminal Judge Leader (or Warrior? I don't recall off the top of my head).</div> </div> </div> </div>Awwww. But if those are two distinct Callings, they probably are not interchangeable. While these archetypes might overlap - so do Guardian and Warrior. Say, Gwyn ap Nudd is a liminal figure, Eris is a trickster... but Loki or Hermes are definitely both. Why choose between two awesome Callings when you can have both, if they fit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T03:51:24-07:00","id":921928,"title":"","content":"Netjer<br /> <br /> Re- Leader, Liminal, Creator<br /> Osiris- Liminal, Leader, Sage (last one is definitely a stretch)<br /> Ptah- Creator, Sage definitely but the last one alludes me, Leader/guardian?<br /> Isis- Sage, Healer, Trickster <br /> Anubis-Judge, Liminal, Guardian<br /> Bast- Guardian, Warrior, Hunter<br /> Set-Trickster, Guardian, Warrior<br /> Horus- Warrior, Leader, Hunter<br /> Hathor- Lover, Warrior, Healer (I always felt Hathor should have been more prominent since she was such a Huge goddess to the ancient Egyptians)<br /> Thoth- Sage, Judge, Guardian<br /> <br /> I left out the more primordial gods; Nut, Geb, and Sobek while widely worshiped they feel less like gods and more forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T17:47:14-07:00","id":1216399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/908618-2e-let-s-try-and-guess-callings?p=908804#post908804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no,he didnt loved no one,he raped people. you gotta call a duck a duck</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey,i apologize for i said here. Zeus ain't no rapist,thatwas a wrong information i gor from a book. sorry for the trouble","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}